  {
   "id": "var p vs var 1 strategy",
   "nombre_canonico": "VAR(p) vs VAR(1) strategy",
   "tipo": "estrategia",
   "nombres_vistos": [
    "VAR(p) vs VAR(1) strategy"
   ],
   "menciones": 1,
   "doc_frecuencia": 1,
   "doc_ids": [
    326
   ],
   "definiciones": [
    {
     "texto": "Comparación empírica entre la estrategia no Markoviana VAR(p) (con p=15, tres semanas de trading) que incorpora sliding average de precios históricos, y la estrategia Markoviana VAR(1) de Chiu y Wong (2015). La VAR(p) es más agresiva en tendencias y genera retornos anormales con mayor leverage.",
     "doc_id": 326
    }
   ],
   "citas": [
    {
     "texto": "We aim to contrast the non-Markovian equilibrium strategy, which we refer to as the VAR(p) strategy, with its Markovian counterpart in Chiu & Wong (2015), which we refer to as the VAR(1) strategy.",
     "doc_id": 326
    }
